\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Discussion}
\title{Charges on a sum of species}
\date{2026-11-26}

\p{For one species, the inverse of the modified rotation multiplies the
[coefficient functional](fdip-00TJ) by #{u^{-d}} under pullback, by
\ref{fdip-014L}. Each of the two gradings contributes a difference of
dimensions to #{d}. If the different species are rotated by different
integer powers of the same unit, which units fix the joint functional?
When does a whole cyclic group of rotations fix it?}
